    "explanation": "Both accounts are measured against the same record, and the arithmetic is not seriously in dispute. POL-NS-01 requires four things and all four hold on the driver's own instrument evidence. (a) The trip record carries a driver 'arrived' event at 08:10:20. (b) The GPS trace places the driver inside the pickup geofence at and before that moment: all 33 of his fixes sit 24.0 m from the pin with 0.0 km/h recorded throughout, so the three-consecutive-qualifying-fix test under POL-NS-02 is met inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius. (c) The continuous in-geofence dwell runs from the first qualifying fix at 08:10:00 to the cancellation at 08:15:20 — 320 seconds, measured from the fix and not from the 'arrived' tap, against the 300-second STANDARD minimum: 20 seconds to spare. (d) The trip was terminated by the driver at 08:15:20, after the required dwell elapsed at 08:15:00, with cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW and no boarding event. The rider's request that the 320-second run be verified against the qualifying-fix rules has been checked and it qualifies as stated.\n\nNothing from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces the fee. The arrival marker is not false under POL-NS-05: at 08:10:20 the driver was 24.0 m from the pin and stationary, neither more than 300 m away nor travelling at 15 km/h or above — he was in the geofence 20 seconds before he tapped. This is not a wrong-entrance case under POL-NS-03, because that clause operates only where the driver is stationary outside the arrival radius but within 400 m of the pin, and every qualifying fix here is inside the radius. POL-NS-06 finds no shortfall to refund: 320 seconds exceeds the 300-second minimum, so there is no waiting-period failure however one views the rider's presence.\n\nThe traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-09101-01 is MISSING (no payload; weight 0.0), so POL-NS-06 limb (i) accumulation across separate intervals is unavailable and was not asserted. Its absence changes nothing here: the single uninterrupted interval already satisfies the minimum, and a traffic advisory can never reduce the required minimum in any event. That omitted artifact is the only impaired item on the record and the ruling does not rely on it.\n\nThe rider's POL-NS-04 route is not available, and the rider properly does not press it. Limb (a) fails because the chat log — 3 messages, matching trip_record.chat_message_count of 3 — contains only the system arrival notice at 08:10:21 and the driver's two messages at 08:10:35 and 08:14:10; the rider sent no locating or coordinating message. Limb (c) fails in any event: the rider's device track records no qualifying fix inside the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius, all 15 fixes sitting 519.4 m from the pin. The rider's assertion that he 'was downstairs' is not supported by his own device track, which places him roughly 519 m away throughout the window; but under POL-NS-06 the waiting-period test turns on the driver's in-geofence dwell whether or not the rider was present, so the rider's position does not by itself decide the fee. The rider's related point — that his own position cannot justify the charge — is correct as a matter of law, and it does not help him, because the charge is independently justified on the driver's arrival and dwell facts.\n\nThe evidence is clean for integrity purposes. The trace has 100% coverage, 33 fixes at the emitted 10-second cadence and a maximum gap of 0 seconds; the chat log holds the 3 messages the trip record records; and the arrived (08:10:20) and cancellation (08:15:20) timestamps both coincide with trace fixes, so there is no clock skew under POL-NS-08(a), no trace defect under (b), no chat defect under (c) and no fare defect under (d). The SGD 4.00 cancellation fee is the GREATER of the STANDARD zone-class fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00), and it matches total_charged of SGD 4.00. No POL-NS-09 trigger is engaged: confidence is above the 0.70 floor; no two admissible artifacts contradict each other on arrival, dwell or rider presence; the same rider and driver show 0 disputes in the trailing 90 days; the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip (no_show_terminations_30d is 1, below 4, and 1 ÷ 120 completed trips is about 0.008, below 0.08); and the deciding facts rest on unimpaired artifacts.\n\nOutcome. POL-NS-01 being satisfied in full and nothing displacing it, the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee stands exactly as charged on this rider-filed dispute (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00), and the driver is paid 80% of that fee under POL-NS-07 — SGD 3.20 of SGD 4.00 — with the residual SGD 0.80 retained as the platform service fee. Because the ruling moves money to the driver, the ruling value is DRIVER_COMPENSATION and amount_sgd mirrors driver_compensation_sgd at SGD 3.20; this is not a refund to the rider. No referral is produced: POL-NS-05(ii)'s false-arrival record does not apply because no false marker was found, and the POL-NS-07 anti-farming escalation did not trip."
